# API Endpoints Reference

## Overview
This document defines the standard API endpoint patterns and structure for Express.js backend applications.
All API module endpoints **must** use the `/api/v1/` base path prefix as required by `api.mdc`.

## 0. System Health Endpoints (Unversioned)
These endpoints are **system endpoints** and are not mounted under `/api/v1` (see `health-checks.mdc`):
```javascript
GET /health
GET /ready
GET /live
```

## 1. Authentication & User Management
```javascript
/api/v1/auth/
├── POST /login                    // Authenticate user and return JWT
├── POST /register                 // Register new user account
├── POST /verify-email             // Verify email with token/code
├── POST /verify-phone             // Verify phone with token
├── POST /forgot-password          // Send password reset email
├── POST /reset-password           // Reset password with token
├── POST /change-password           // Change password (authenticated)
├── POST /refresh                  // Refresh JWT token
├── POST /logout                   // Logout and invalidate session
├── GET /me                        // Get current user info
└── POST /resend-verification      // Resend verification email/SMS

/api/v1/users/
├── GET /                          // List users with pagination
├── POST /                         // Create user (admin only)
├── GET /{id}                      // Get user by ID
├── PUT /{id}                      // Update user
├── DELETE /{id}                   // Soft delete user
├── GET /{id}/orders               // Get user's orders
├── GET /{id}/carts                // Get user's carts
├── GET /{id}/favorites            // Get user's favorites
├── GET /{id}/addresses            // Get user's addresses
├── GET /{id}/notifications        // Get user's notifications
├── GET /{id}/sessions             // Get user's sessions
├── GET /{id}/api-keys             // Get user's API keys
├── GET /{id}/subscriptions        // Get user's subscriptions
├── GET /{id}/consents             // Get user's consents
└── GET /{id}/audit-logs           // Get user's audit logs
```

